From: Precision GPU maintenance
Subject: [UNVALIDATED CANDIDATE] Skip GPU blit into scanout-only buffers

The previous physical test aborted in Mesa iris submission after importing a
NVIDIA dumb buffer into Intel for a GPU blit. PRIMARY alone still attempts that
path and its asynchronous failure cannot use the synchronous CPU fallback.
Use Mutter's existing explicit CPU-copy flag for this opt-in device only.
This does not change Intel compositing, host applications' rendering, or any
GPU lifetime/handoff logic. Physical output/performance remain unvalidated.

--- a/src/backends/native/meta-renderer-native.c
+++ b/src/backends/native/meta-renderer-native.c
@@ -2077,11 +2077,15 @@ create_renderer_gpu_data_gbm (MetaRendererNative *renderer_native,
   if (meta_kms_device_get_flags (meta_gpu_kms_get_kms_device (gpu_kms)) &
       META_KMS_DEVICE_FLAG_SCANOUT_ONLY)
     {
-      /* Avoid even a speculative secondary GBM import/allocation. The primary
-       * GPU copies to a dumb scanout buffer, with the existing CPU fallback.
+      /* Do not submit Intel GPU work against a NVIDIA-allocated buffer. An
+       * import may succeed but submission can fail asynchronously, beyond
+       * the synchronous GPU-blit fallback. Read pixels into the dumb buffer.
        */
       renderer_gpu_data->secondary.copy_mode =
         META_SHARED_FRAMEBUFFER_COPY_MODE_PRIMARY;
+      renderer_gpu_data->secondary.copy_mode_primary_force_cpu = TRUE;
+      g_message ("Using CPU copy for scanout-only device '%s'",
+                 meta_gpu_kms_get_file_path (gpu_kms));
       return renderer_gpu_data;
     }
 
